  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Heleniamarin may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through its target proteins, Phosphodiesterase 6C, Methyl 9-cyclopropylnonanoate, and Broussoaurone A. These compounds are all identified as targets of Heleniamarin, and each of them is linked to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of molecular interactions. The scores assigned to these relationships are consistent, indicating a potential biological relevance. The shared mechanism of interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex suggests that Heleniamarin may modulate the activity of this chromatin-modifying complex, potentially through the regulation of its target proteins. The evidence is robust and consistent across multiple paths, supporting a plausible relationship between Heleniamarin and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. However, further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional role of Heleniamarin in this pathway.",
